  "slug": "collector-leader-leases-and-subscriber-handoff-recovery",
  "concept": "Collector leader leases and subscriber handoff recovery",
  "generated": "2026-11-12",
  "summary": "Source-anchored research for Collector leader leases and subscriber handoff recovery. Run status: COMPLETED.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A collector lease does not by itself prevent an expired owner from continuing work. Process pauses can produce overlapping leaders; Kubernetes client-go explicitly disclaims fencing. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://github.com/kubernetes/client-go/blob/master/tools/leaderelection/leaderelection.go",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e32772d424a9419e8d1ff7aa46a22f7db70ef0309d593417f5e167439ae9a2d8",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:90580155cbe47ca1309f840c59492ef8c03510d99b2a1d06de7e6748464df7ce",
            "ev:efd4431eb31cdbcc1cb87f24f97ecb487e6a677ce8c5ed9b11e4ce6729ff15ea"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/nijatsdev/redlease",
            "https://aws.amazon.com/builders-library/leader-election-in-distributed-systems/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When client-go ReleaseOnCancel is enabled, all lease-guarded work must finish before cancelling the election context; its source warns that otherwise two processes may act on the critical path. For a graceful collector handoff, drain or terminate guarded work before releasing ownership. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://github.com/kubernetes/client-go/blob/master/tools/leaderelection/leaderelection.go",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b504030836bd015824b97631ea0b97d32eb288a815277656ac92fd9f8496ed39",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:07479900391319b468f992d33900ba12116d597d06806fa6855936f7a13e5f85"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Recommended handoff invariant: make event processing durable before advancing the recoverable replay checkpoint, and make replayed processing idempotent. This applies Amazon’s durability-before-completion rule to Salesforce’s process-then-commit protocol; it is a design inference, not a Salesforce transaction guarantee. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://aws.amazon.com/builders-library/leader-election-in-distributed-systems/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b5dcc4830759094ce7d119245f9baaf6cd43c64c19c76541d6e3111deefc108d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:6e29794fb92e685e46aeb1681a9d75543cfa71db943213c6462663881a71cd67",
            "ev:cdc0f85796b915d9ec8c7397efa9b665af51b62c90113f33400e169cd09cd7f8"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/managedsubscribe-rpc.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The redlease implementation warns that asynchronous Redis replication can lose an acknowledged token increment during failover. Its token monotonicity is therefore not a failover-safe guarantee; use a linearizable token authority when that guarantee is required. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://github.com/nijatsdev/redlease",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:110879247b7793ec9fa545349d7614f945d0fc2177393a0a73101dbf05606274",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:15cc107cfc15b875bf492e9a1b475d0ed0b37121be549ef1df9e3a0945324417",
            "ev:caf520f571399f7429187cbf04847abf0e2f9cf79d4be1eb085979cf85a7f49b"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How-to and procedures",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "To resume a normal Salesforce subscription after handoff, use CUSTOM with the replay ID of the last keepalive or processed event, whichever arrived last; store the opaque ID as bytes. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a4f96182e0d4dc4f5d5b4e9f6a24786f5fa8ea306ab1d3634209342f597ae1c1",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:4308b25f87bbfead6a265033c8b4cc7c2ac5af37332ef5ebc3289598c20abf85"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Kleppmann’s fencing pattern assigns an increasing token on each lock acquisition and requires the storage service to reject writes with older tokens. A collector design can apply this pattern to prevent a resumed former owner from overwriting a newer owner’s state; a lease check in the process alone cannot close the pause-before-write race. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://martin.kleppmann.com/2016/02/08/how-to-do-distributed-locking.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:6f5c28bf920c6a0c66afee7c1e517632d2f024db7f7628e7975b9c4dcaa1e039",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2cfdf767da40636d2b4d4fc501ade7bcf069bd6e5ac5a686e4940e0e8d4ddbae",
            "ev:588685c365a6ffdbde0e095725f2a2cb8147acb7e6eac584044a72718dbeca91"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/nijatsdev/redlease"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Salesforce documents a normal 72-hour event-retention window, but rare org moves can reset retained streams and make events inaccessible. Replay catch-up requires retained history; EARLIEST retrieves retained events and cannot restore already-purged history. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/event-message-durability.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:5e63163af0193dcc68549b7e285da60e88584db44f8b407e09b25022953fd9bd",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3769bffd1b267d86d8c703ac69b3abd479e12bf41428319c1c2fd9d5f6b77c4c",
            "ev:5ec948f6f071f6d6662dacdb7fc9562ac46c0455c7c534800bdf0fffcf3f938e",
            "ev:bfb10fc8df18c0293c529bbdfb6dbe976eed7cd2675b0f2046261b006bce7643"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "ManagedSubscribe resumes from the last successfully committed Replay ID when the client reconnects with the same subscription ID. Processing precedes committing, and CommitReplayResponse reports success or failure; sending a commit request alone does not establish a persisted checkpoint. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/managedsubscribe-rpc.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7d5e8cd1857d80d8186451eb1f58d8d474588ff2d2abf1ba6c8272a0c9c7cd93",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:16d2ed5d26896377691c6a7bbf70eeed32e1c4909ffcccddb6a507f207cfea95",
            "ev:6e29794fb92e685e46aeb1681a9d75543cfa71db943213c6462663881a71cd67",
            "ev:dece6ba8e1584370eacc568ad3bd0b85dcbf2100067923ec89b666b4be8d8af7"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/managed-sub.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Salesforce documents a managed subscription as unique per client and says it cannot be shared with other clients in the same org. Server-side replay storage therefore must not be assumed to provide a general multi-client leader-election or fencing protocol. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/managed-sub.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:8cff2b520fa2b8ccc46287066022ce4373025f3e31cb0e539fa090e0214288cc",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:64c316bdcae98245f984627bb7cae0e8254ee3bbaecc59641d1786a2119f0673",
            "ev:d60fa80c6628335e807db49ec2da2f37e87e7beef8c8d87ccc2ecb4d61e1a97c"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/managedsubscribe-rpc.html"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Do not use an administrative ManagedEventSubscription STOP/RUN cycle as a cursor-preserving handoff: STOP deletes the previously committed Replay ID, and a later restart begins from defaultReplay rather than the former checkpoint. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/managed-sub.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:3f6f0a52eece589173ca1461d4e96b2bdec3c74d2197fd8fcacd1feecc1c8615",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2039d485d276d1b75ef6f188a3ed344d32a95c74c23e26fa61b1da4d4c196681"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "With Subscribe, the successor can create a new RPC using CUSTOM and the stored replay_id to resume after that position. Preserve replay IDs as opaque bytes rather than calculating the next ID. Replay options are read from the first FetchRequest; changing position requires a new Subscribe call. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:10d7c2b23ee3b08e8b59dc2305791e1186abbc3f937f41c162b32c16c7a8bb3f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:15c6a156d12b27a3d0a3aff8ce446eef480235eb789698565dbc80f200b96797",
            "ev:1b261bd6187df8f3a87e3099aadb6dea27263e1098ee49cbffb8b7f76ac94eca",
            "ev:8cbedad7368e944f052ec5618dedea9ea9fa74e34d2ad48af0298b2290781203"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/event-message-durability.html"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "For an idle Subscribe stream, Salesforce recommends saving the replay_id from empty keepalive responses for resubscription. As a collector safety inference, advance that checkpoint only after all earlier delivered work is durable, so a crash does not skip pending work. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:dad217d2542fab6f414d1068ada5d7db6627eac749ef2bd3763ceaec4039f8b7",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:a7ed09bc7a378c3c59960ccb0d0d5732d14c43a5c887c3f354abf0b976ad3280",
            "ev:cdc0f85796b915d9ec8c7397efa9b665af51b62c90113f33400e169cd09cd7f8"
          ],
